---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

const tags = ["Campaign Strategy", "Paid Social", "Influencer Marketing", "Customer Acquisition", "Social Media"];

const pillars = [
  {
    name: "Proof of Impact",
    body: "Field stories, photos and the 100% model that show exactly where every dollar goes.",
  },
  {
    name: "The Current on Campus",
    body: "Student voices and simple ways to start or join the movement at your school.",
  },
  {
    name: "Water, Explained",
    body: "Quick, shareable facts on the global water crisis and why it matters to your generation.",
  },
];

const posts = [
  {
    pillar: "Proof of Impact",
    caption:
      "Ever wonder where your donation actually goes? With The Current, 100% of your gift funds a clean water project, and we show you the proof. Start giving $1 a month, link in bio. #charitywater",
  },
  {
    pillar: "The Current on Campus",
    caption:
      "Clean water, powered by students like you. The Current is a $1-a-month movement you can bring to your own campus. Tap the link in bio to join. #charitywater",
  },
  {
    pillar: "Water, Explained",
    caption:
      "696 million people still live without clean water. The good news: change can cost as little as $1 a month. Learn the facts and join The Current, link in bio. #charitywater",
  },
];

const criteria = [
  "Reaches the audience: a mostly US, Gen Z college following, ideally at activism-minded campuses.",
  "Fits the cause: posts about activism, sustainability, nonprofits or campus life, so clean water feels natural, not random.",
  "Authentic and engaged: a micro-influencer with roughly 10,000 to 100,000 followers, high engagement and real values, so the $1-a-month ask reads as a genuine recommendation rather than an ad.",
];

const ideas = [
  "A Walk for Water on the quad, where students carry jerry cans the distance many kids walk each day for water, then sign up for The Current right after.",
  "A pop-up refill and clean-water tasting station at club fairs and orientation, staffed by student ambassadors who explain the $1-a-month program.",
  "A $1 Challenge with student orgs and Greek life, where chapters compete to recruit the most monthly givers to The Current.",
];
---

<Base
  title="charity: water: Activating the Next Generation of Supporters | Grace Joy Park"
  description="Grace Joy Park's customer-acquisition case study: a $1-a-month student donation campaign for charity: water, built through the Global Career Accelerator across organic social, influencer, paid social and campus activation."
>
  <p class="back"><a href="/work">&larr; Back to Work</a></p>

  <article class="post">
    <h1>charity: water: Activating the Next Generation of Supporters</h1>
    <p class="meta muted">The Global Career Accelerator &middot; July 2026 &middot; Digital Marketing</p>

    <ul class="tags">
      {tags.map((t) => <li>{t}</li>)}
    </ul>

    <div class="prose">
      <p class="lede">
        I built a customer-acquisition campaign to bring college students into charity:
        water as recurring donors. charity: water is a real nonprofit, but this was a
        capstone I developed through the Global Career Accelerator, not a live initiative
        for the organization. I owned the positioning and the full funnel, from organic
        social and influencer strategy to paid social and a campus ambassador program.
      </p>

      <p class="deck-link">
        <a href="/charity-water-deck.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View the full project deck (PDF) &rarr;</a>
      </p>

      <h2>The positioning</h2>
      <p>
        charity: water&rsquo;s recurring program, The Spring, asks for an open-ended monthly
        gift, which feels out of reach on a student budget. I built the campaign around The
        Current, a $1-a-month program tied to a student-led movement, so giving reads as
        affordable, social and made for the activism-minded college audience I was trying to
        reach. That reframing sits at the top of the landing page and carries through every
        channel below.
      </p>

      <h2>Organic social</h2>
      <p>
        I built the Instagram presence at <strong>@jointhecurrent</strong> around three
        content pillars, each aimed at a different reason a student might give:
      </p>
      <ul class="pillars-grid">
        {pillars.map((p) => (
          <li class="pillar">
            <span class="pillar-name">{p.name}</span>
            <p>{p.body}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p>
        Then I wrote a post for each pillar, keeping the copy short, hopeful and built around
        the $1-a-month ask:
      </p>
      <ul class="posts-grid">
        {posts.map((p) => (
          <li class="post-card">
            <span class="post-pillar">{p.pillar}</span>
            <p>{p.caption}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <h2>Influencer marketing</h2>
      <p>
        For influencer work I wrote the content guidelines first: a short, personal TikTok
        about why the creator gives to clean water, ending with an invite to join The Current
        for $1 a month. Each post had to show the creator on camera, real charity: water
        project footage, the $1-a-month ask and the @jointhecurrent handle on screen, in a
        tone that stays hopeful and genuine and focuses on the good a dollar can do. I then
        set the criteria I used to pick creators:
      </p>
      <ul class="criteria">
        {criteria.map((c) => <li>{c}</li>)}
      </ul>

      <h2>Paid social</h2>
      <p>
        On the paid side I built an interest-based audience to introduce The Current to
        college students who do not know it yet and drive first-time sign-ups.
      </p>
      <div class="kpi">
        <div class="kpi-row"><span class="kpi-label">Objective</span><span>First-time $1-a-month sign-ups from a cold college audience</span></div>
        <div class="kpi-row"><span class="kpi-label">KPI</span><span>New $1-a-month sign-ups, working toward a goal of 2,000 student donors</span></div>
        <div class="kpi-row"><span class="kpi-label">Efficiency metric</span><span>Cost per sign-up, or total ad spend divided by new $1-a-month donors</span></div>
      </div>
      <p>
        To make the spend work harder, I paired that with a retargeting audience of people
        who visited the landing page or engaged with a post but did not sign up. They already
        showed interest, so a simple reminder of the $1-a-month ask and the 100% model gives
        them a low-pressure reason to finish. Because they are already warm and cost little to
        reach again, they are the audience most likely to convert.
      </p>

      <h2>Campus activation</h2>
      <p>
        The last piece was a student ambassador program, modeled on how brands like Red Bull
        and Amazon Prime Student win students early and keep them for years. I proposed three
        on-campus activations to turn attention into sign-ups:
      </p>
      <ul class="ideas">
        {ideas.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}
      </ul>
    </div>

    <section class="why-section">
      <h2>What I Learned</h2>
      <p>
        Building the campaign end to end taught me how a single idea, a $1-a-month gift, can
        hold a whole funnel together when the organic posts, the influencer brief, the paid
        targeting and the campus events all repeat it in their own way. The hardest and most
        useful part was writing for a specific audience: everything had to sound affordable and
        student-led, because that reframing was the entire reason the campaign could work.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .back { margin-bottom: 1rem; font-size: 0.95rem; }

  .post h1 {
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .meta {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .tags {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem;
  }

  .tags li {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.15rem 0.7rem;
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .prose p {
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .prose .lede {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
  }

  .deck-link {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .pillars-grid {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .pillar {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  .pillar-name {
    display: block;
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .pillar p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .posts-grid {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .post-card {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 1rem;
    background: #f3efe6;
  }

  .post-pillar {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .post-card p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .criteria,
  .ideas {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .criteria li,
  .ideas li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .kpi {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 0.5rem 1rem;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .kpi-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.6rem 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .kpi-row + .kpi-row {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .kpi-label {
    flex: 0 0 9rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    padding-top: 0.15rem;
  }

  .why-section {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .why-section h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  .why-section p {
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .pillars-grid,
    .posts-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .kpi-row {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.2rem;
    }
    .kpi-label {
      flex-basis: auto;
    }
  }
</style>
